upplies no decision\nrule, inventory fact, target architecture, sensory inference, candidate\nranking, experimental method, or answer to the attached case.\n\nMuseum catalogues sometimes describe per\nINTERVENTION END\n\nCASE START\nA client asks for a DHP-level Cypress perfume and insists that depth requires at least forty materials. The desired smell is luxurious, intimate, and floral, with high-quality French Cypress EO as the subject, but not a literal forest. Current ready candidates include Cypress EO, Magnolia EO, Alpha Irone 10% w/w in DEP, Orris Liquid 30% w/w, Hedione, Florol, Alpha Ionone, Hexyl Salicylate, Habanolide, Romandolide, Ambrettolide 10%, and Ethylene Brassylate. No blinded sensory or preference observations exist. Decide the architecture; do not write a dose formula.\nCASE END\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object and no prose outside it. Use this schema:\n{\n  \"case_id\": \"<exact case id>\",\n  \"decision\": \"THEORY_SELECTED|FRONTIER|HOLD|NO_CHANGE\",\n  \"target_ideal\": {\n    \"identity\": \"<locked target independent of inventory>\",\n    \"primary_subject\": \"<subject>\",\n    \"supporting_architecture\": [\"<explicit relational registers>\"],\n    \"forbidden_drift\": [\"<specific failure modes>\"]\n  },\n  \"current_inventory_build\": {\n    \"status\": \"READY|HOLD|NOT_APPLICABLE\",\n    \"usable_materials\": [\"<current exact identities only>\"],\n    \"held_or_unavailable\": [\"<identity: reason>\"],\n    \"target_changed_by_inventory\": false\n  },\n  \"relations\": [\n    {\n      \"relation\": \"<source to target and mechanism>\",\n      \"target_link\": \"<why required>\",\n      \"omission_loss\": \"<specific loss>\",\n      \"failure_mode\": \"<takeover or collision>\",\n      \"temporal_windows\": [\"<window>\"],\n      \"controlled_comparison\": \"<constant-total discriminating arm>\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": {\n    \"computational_design\": \"SUPPORTED|HOLD|NOT_APPLICABLE\",\n    \"temporal_sensory\": \"OBSERVED|WITHHE