nd Cypress registers would sit beside each other with less integration, dimensionality, and luxurious inwardness.\",\n      \"failure_mode\": \"The bridge can become powdery, cosmetic, violet-dominant, or independently orris-like.\",\n      \"temporal_windows\": [\n        \"early heart\",\n        \"heart\",\n        \"early drydown\"\n      ],\n      \"controlled_comparison\": \"Compare the complete architecture with a constant-total arm in which the entire orris-violet bridge is replaced by carrier, holding Cypress, floral support, musk structure, and total material load constant.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation\": \"Hexyl Salicylate to the floral and orris-violet registers through a slower floral-body bridge into the base.\",\n      \"target_link\": \"The relation can extend floral continuity and prevent an abrupt break between the luminous heart and intimate drydown.\",\n      \"omission_loss\": \"The floral heart may thin or disconnect before the musk-supported drydown develops.\",\n      \"failure_mode\": \"Excess floral body can blur Cypress articulation or make the heart broad and generic.\",\n      \"temporal_windows\": [\n        \"heart\",\n        \"early drydown\"\n      ],\n      \"controlled_comparison\": \"Compare otherwise identical constant-total arms with the floral-body bridge present versus replaced by carrier, preserving the Cypress subject and every other register.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"relation\": \"Habanolide, Romandolide, Ambrettolide 10%, and Ethylene Brassylate to the Cypress-floral structure through a layered intimate diffusion and persistence envelope.\",\n      \"target_link\": \"The target requires intimacy and luxury across time, so the base must carry the Cypress-floral identity without substituting generic musk volume for depth.\",\n      \"omission_loss\": \"The architecture may lose skin proximity, temporal continuity, and a coherent drydown around the primary subject.\",\n      \"failure_mode\": \"The musk envelope can b